REM Protects a bare RETURN used to exit a multi-line DEF FN body early,
REM before the value-carrying RETURN that ends the function, from being
REM flagged as an error for lacking a return value. Covers both the
REM in-loop early-exit shape and a single-line IF guard shape, in upper
REM and lower case.
DEF FNGREATESTCOMMONFACTOR(numone, numtwo)
    IF numone = 0 THEN RETURN
    WHILE numone <> 0
        temp = numone, numone = MOD(numtwo, numone), numtwo = temp
    WEND
    RETURN numtwo
FNEND
def fnfirstpositive(itemone, itemtwo)
    if itemone > 0 then return
    return itemtwo
fnend
